  [RISK] arch/riscv/include/asm/insn.h:412-412  SET_RD
      SET_RD is a pure write-only assignment — `*REG_PTR(insn, SH_RD, regs) = (val)` — with no read of the prior register value. This is the canonical 'overwrite' primitive. Using SET_RD directly for a PM4 accumulating multiply-add instruction (instead of a read-modify-write sequence: GET_RS1 + compute + SET_RD) is the exact code-level manifestation of the spec violation. The macro itself is not buggy; it is correct for its intended purpose (non-accumulating instructions). The risk is that a future PM4 handler author uses SET_RD as the sole rd write without first reading the prior rd value, silently discarding accumulator state.
