      CSR instruction emulation correctly models the accumulating-vs-overwriting distinction via wr_mask/new_val pairs: CSRRW uses wr_mask=-1UL,new_val=rs1_val (full overwrite); CSRRS uses wr_mask=rs1_val,new_val=-1UL (read-modify-write, set bits where rs1 has 1s); CSRRC uses wr_mask=rs1_val,new_val=0 (read-modify-write, clear bits where rs1 has 1s). This correctly preserves prior CSR state in read-modify-write variants. Serves as a reference implementation: a correct PM4 handler must analogously distinguish accumulating variants (read prior rd, sum product, write back) from non-accumulating variants (compute result, overwrite rd).
